{"authored" [{"question" "q-351430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=16-9{t}^{2}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=3$ and $t=4.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=3$ and $t=4.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(16-9{t}^{2})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & ={(16t-3{t}^{3})|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =[16(4)-3(4)^{3}]-[16(3)-3(3)^{3}] \\\\  & =[64-192]-[48-81] \\\\  & =-95.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ the particle is located at the position $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{2}+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=3{e}^{3t-1}.$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2{e}^{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(5) & =2{e}^{2}+{\\int }_{1}^{5}3{e}^{3t-1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+{[{e}^{3t-1}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+({e}^{3(5)-1}-{e}^{3(1)-1}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+({e}^{14}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}-{e}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+{e}^{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x={e}^{2}+{e}^{14}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{14}-{e}^{2}+1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{16}-{e}^{2}+1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2}+{e}^{16}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "061f82368c0ad399fc2bf18b51ced8b9d4a32f295ab3a44387b7cb5a30574ada" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 2t + 3t^2.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "902c39eabe7fa5fcd71f6ab8a5ed2992b55ce2683462c85bb8214aade1abfe5e" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2t+3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={({t}^{2}+{t}^{3})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}+{3}^{3}]-[{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =[9+27]-[1+1] \\\\  & =36-2 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=3$ is $34.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "902c39eabe7fa5fcd71f6ab8a5ed2992b55ce2683462c85bb8214aade1abfe5e" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^2 +4t.$ At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-20.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf39f066a9bebfa423e36e53e5d26410735ad5e78e6a00d4cf8f063443a3f4c3" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in[2,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4) = x(2) + \\int_2^4 v(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(4) & =-20+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =-20+{[2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-20+([2(4)^{3}+2(4)^{2}]-[2(2)^{3}+2(2)^{2}]) \\\\  & =-20+([128+32]-[16+8]) \\\\  & =-20+(160-24) \\\\  & =-20+136 \\\\  & =116.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=116.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf39f066a9bebfa423e36e53e5d26410735ad5e78e6a00d4cf8f063443a3f4c3" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "d2c6d2782d678e247239b6b0463883ecc5c6091a11425d6c62613dbf202fecf5" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t = 8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8) = x(2)+ \\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-1$, and we can compute the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt = 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8) = -1+ 6 = 5\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "d2c6d2782d678e247239b6b0463883ecc5c6091a11425d6c62613dbf202fecf5" "basis" 1190 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}-2t.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{t}^{2}-2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[2(4)^{3}-(4)^{2}]-[2(1)^{3}-(1)^{2}] \\\\  & =[128-16]-[2-1] \\\\  & =112-1 \\\\  & =111.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=4$ is $111.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "b