f61f0d8f875ad0cb03b35d4037e75c227d4523502193.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(1)=2,$ and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=1$ to $t=5.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(5)=2+6=8.\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3098db78f821b58a903233efdfa698212d95480b32bc5b7c852fddd5ef3cbf4b" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9709dbf4b4dab3618c7bc97b3fefbdecbf04e55c3c9723c120eb446d2a9caea" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 2t + 3t^2.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "b8898e26a80178eac6b570ed5da3c8ff2273acceb8265730797b7a0cb2b7f102" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2t+3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={({t}^{2}+{t}^{3})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}+{3}^{3}]-[{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =[9+27]-[1+1] \\\\  & =36-2 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=3$ is $34.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "b8898e26a80178eac6b570ed5da3c8ff2273acceb8265730797b7a0cb2b7f102" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^2 +4t.$ At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-20.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf5431d28318289d2b378f362fd185a578fd2d6248ac545fb395229c648236eb" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in[2,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4) = x(2) + \\int_2^4 v(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(4) & =-20+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =-20+{[2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-20+([2(4)^{3}+2(4)^{2}]-[2(2)^{3}+2(2)^{2}]) \\\\  & =-20+([128+32]-[16+8]) \\\\  & =-20+(160-24) \\\\  & =-20+136 \\\\  & =116.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=116.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf5431d28318289d2b378f362fd185a578fd2d6248ac545fb395229c648236eb" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "863e847ff57a5694a6c8facc39dacc346c93ec5ce1d87b780d9cc602d90aaaa5" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t = 8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8) = x(2)+ \\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-1$, and we can compute the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt = 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8) = -1+ 6 = 5\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "863e847ff57a5694a6c8facc39dacc346c93ec5ce1d87b780d9cc602d90aaaa5" "basis" 1525 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-348281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}-4t.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=0$ and $t=5.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-348281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=5.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}(6{t}^{2}-4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(2{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =[2(5)^{3}-2(5)^{2}]-[2(0)^{3}-2(0)^{2}] \\\\  & =[250-50]-0 \\\\  & =200.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-348281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-348281" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-348281" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "200"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=0$ and $t=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=1.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(t)){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-351442" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351442" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=16-9{t}^{2}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=3$ and $t=4.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=3$ and $t=4.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(16-9{t}^{2})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & ={(16t-3{t}^{3})|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =[16(4)-3(4)^{3}]-[16(3)-3(3)^{3}] \\\\  & =[64-192]-[48-81] \\\\  & =-95.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-95"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=-4t-1.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=0$ and $t=1.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=1.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-4t-1)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(-2{t}^{2}-t){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[-2(1)^{2}-(1)]-[-2(0)^{2}-(0)] \\\\  & =[-2-1]-0 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-351420" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351420" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}-2t.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{t}^{2}-2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[2(4)^{3}-(4)^{2}]-[2(1)^{3}-(1)^{2}] \\\\  & =[128-16]-[2-1] \\\\  & =112-1 \\\\  & =111.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=4$ is $111.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "111"] ["math" "148"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "88"] ["math" "92"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "111"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}+4t.$ At time $t=4$ the particle is located at the position $x=-300.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=4$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [4,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(4)+{\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(7) & =-300+{\\int }_{4}^{7}(6{t}^{2}+4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =-300+{[2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2})]}_{4}^{7} \\\\  & =-300+([2(7)^{3}+2(7)^{2}]-[2(4)^{3}+2(4)^{2}]) \\\\  & =-300+([686+98]-[128+32]) \\\\  & =-300+(784-160) \\\\  & =-300+624 \\\\  & =324.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=324.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-2417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "214"] ["math" "221"] ["math" "269"] ["math" "324"] ["math" "453"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-2417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "324"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ the particle is located at the position $x=5.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi .$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =5+{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5+{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =5+[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )]-[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =5+(0-1)-(1+0) \\\\  & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-351448" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351448" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ the particle is located at the position $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{2}+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)={e}^{t-1}.$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=2$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,2].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(2)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{2}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) & =2+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2+{[{e}^{t-1}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2+({e}^{2-1}-{e}^{1-1}) \\\\  & =2+({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =2+e-1 \\\\  & =e+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=2$ is $x=e+1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-84265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2e"] ["math" "2e+1"] ["math" "e"] ["math" "e+1"] ["math" "e+2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e+1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=3{e}^{3t-1}.$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2{e}^{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(5) & =2{e}^{2}+{\\int }_{1}^{5}3{e}^{3t-1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+{[{e}^{3t-1}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+({e}^{3(5)-1}-{e}^{3(1)-1}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+({e}^{14}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}-{e}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+{e}^{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x={e}^{2}+{e}^{14}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75c