$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{3}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=3$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=3+8=11.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=11.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-351472" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-351472" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/assets/2743c66fc9181611e3095b736d7d5021e43eafcd2e6639766ef5e65fa7779018.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=6?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=6$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,6].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(6)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(1)=1$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{1}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=1$ to $t=6.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(6)=1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=\\frac{3}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-84316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["ma