=9$ is $x=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/assets/18904539463b95f9d681f61f0d8f875ad0cb03b35d4037e75c227d4523502193.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(1)=2,$ and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=1$ to $t=5.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(5)=2+6=8.\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-121011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/assets/b2fbcc246230bd88e58d7928384a6d09966e37af63879775470fb58dd5005582.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At the time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=4.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(1)=4,$ and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{1}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=1$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=4+(-3)=1\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a8bebd9dd930cdfcc6bbd159681e2b7c867fa8ffdb50b4783eb7f8807706a9c"} {"question" "q-84315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "q-84315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/state.json" "file_sha256" "d75cdfcf1e1a47fc138d511a274df296f621072509812466e7c88dab73545f52"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 2t + 3t^2.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "b8898e26a80178eac6b570ed5da3c8ff2273acceb8265730797b7a0cb2b7f102"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2t+3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={({t}^{2}+{t}^{3})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}+{3}^{3}]-[{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =[9+27]-[1+1] \\\\  & =36-2 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=3$ is $34.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "b8898e26a80178eac6b570ed5da3c8ff2273acceb8265730797b7a0cb2b7f102"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^2 +4t.$ At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-20.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf5431d28318289d2b378f362fd185a578fd2d6248ac545fb395229c648236eb"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in[2,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4) = x(2) + \\int_2^4 v(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(4) & =-20+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =-20+{[2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-20+([2(4)^{3}+2(4)^{2}]-[2(2)^{3}+2(2)^{2}]) \\\\  & =-20+([128+32]-[16+8]) \\\\  & =-20+(160-24) \\\\  & =-20+136 \\\\  & =116.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=116.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf5431d28318289d2b378f362fd185a578fd2d6248ac545fb395229c648236eb"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "0696ae55a9e4b704ebdbbe79ffe5eabe225d31982d7d86a7c013ea707f8d4ca5"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t = 8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8) = x(2)+ \\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-1$, and we can compute the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt = 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8) = -1+ 6 = 5\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041143/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "0696ae55a9e4b704ebdbbe79ffe5eabe225d31982d7d86a7c013ea707f8d4ca5"}] "usage" {"q-121021" [] "e-712